From 3847c2740ab983a83dc3d4a9dfd379ea69f5929b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 11:07:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06799/11362] Refute wa30 push-not-carry hypothesis (v7 probe)

Walking the player directly into an untouched block only produces a
contact highlight -- no displacement, no push, timer still ticks for
the blocked move. This closes the third and last follow-up hypothesis
from v5's route-computation bound (multi-carry and ACTION6/diagonal
were already refuted in v6). The 80-move optimistic lower bound vs.
the 64-cell L2 timer is now confirmed under every interaction
mechanic tested across 7 attempts; only an untested turn-vs-move cost
split remains as a theoretical way the bound could still be loose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
---
 ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml                    | 15 +++++++++++++++
 results/outer_loop_gpt56sol_wa30_probe_v7.json | 14 ++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 results/outer_loop_gpt56sol_wa30_probe_v7.json

diff --git a/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml b/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
index 922731e7d7..3995bc37a7 100644
--- a/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
+++ b/ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml
@@ -860,6 +860,21 @@ games:
     unexplored: a push-not-carry interaction, or a genuinely different
     turn-vs-move cost split (e.g. reorienting costing 0 vs 1 timer cell
     independent of translating) -- neither tested yet.'
+  - 'v7 (results/outer_loop_gpt56sol_wa30_probe_v7.json): tested the remaining
+    push-not-carry hypothesis directly -- walked the player into an untouched,
+    not-yet-picked-up block''s cell without a prior ACTION5. The block only
+    contact-highlighted (outline color 4 -> 5) in place; neither player nor block
+    entered a new lattice cell, and the timer still ticked (60 -> 59) for the
+    blocked move. REFUTED: wa30 has no push mechanic, only explicit
+    carry-via-ACTION5. Combined with v6, all three follow-up hypotheses
+    (multi-carry, ACTION6/diagonal, push) are now empirically refuted -- the
+    80-move optimistic lower bound vs. the 64-cell L2 timer is confirmed under
+    every interaction mechanic tested. The ONLY remaining untested hypothesis is
+    a turn-vs-move cost split (does reorienting the player without translating
+    cost a separate timer tick from the translate itself, or could a route be
+    restructured to avoid redundant re-orientations the current 80-move Manhattan
+    model implicitly charges for). Absent that, wa30 L2 should be treated as a
+    confirmed dead end for this project''s live-agent mechanics.'
